From: Yury Ilyanok <yuryster@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: phy: aquantia: ensure USXGMII autoneg is enabled on the
 system interface

The AQR113C firmware can come up with the USXGMII autoneg enable bit
(PHY XS Vendor Provisioning 2, 4.0xC441 bit 3) cleared on the system
interface.  When the host PCS runs standard USXGMII autoneg, the
handshake then never completes and the system interface stays down
(4.0xE812 "system interface ready" bit 0 reads 0) even though the line
side trains and links fine - the port passes no traffic in either
direction.

Assert the bit from config_init() whenever the host interface is
USXGMII.  config_init() runs again after PHY resets, so the setting
also survives them.

Signed-off-by: Yury Ilyanok <yuryster@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/phy/aquantia/aquantia.h      |  4 ++++
 drivers/net/phy/aquantia/aquantia_main.c | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 20 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/net/phy/aquantia/aquantia.h
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/aquantia/aquantia.h
@@ -21,6 +21,10 @@
 #define VEND1_GLOBAL_FW_ID_MAJOR		GENMASK(15, 8)
 #define VEND1_GLOBAL_FW_ID_MINOR		GENMASK(7, 0)
 
+/* Vendor specific PHY XS, MDIO_MMD_PHYXS */
+#define MDIO_PHYXS_VEND_PROV2			0xc441
+#define MDIO_PHYXS_VEND_PROV2_USX_AN_EN		BIT(3)
+
 #define VEND1_GLOBAL_MAILBOX_INTERFACE1			0x0200
 #define VEND1_GLOBAL_MAILBOX_INTERFACE1_EXECUTE		BIT(15)
 #define VEND1_GLOBAL_MAILBOX_INTERFACE1_WRITE		BIT(14)
--- a/drivers/net/phy/aquantia/aquantia_main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/aquantia/aquantia_main.c
@@ -616,6 +616,22 @@
 		aqr107_chip_info(phydev);
 
 	/*
+	 * The firmware can come up with USXGMII autoneg disabled on the
+	 * system interface.  The host PCS then never completes the USXGMII
+	 * handshake and the system interface stays down even though the
+	 * line side links fine.  Re-assert the enable bit whenever the host
+	 * interface is USXGMII; config_init runs again after PHY resets, so
+	 * the bit also survives them.
+	 */
+	if (phydev->interface == PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_USXGMII) {
+		ret = phy_set_bits_mmd(phydev, MDIO_MMD_PHYXS,
+				       MDIO_PHYXS_VEND_PROV2,
+				       MDIO_PHYXS_VEND_PROV2_USX_AN_EN);
+		if (ret)
+			return ret;
+	}
+
+	/*
 	 * The board may declare that the host SerDes is fixed at 10GBASE-R
 	 * and cannot follow the firmware's USXGMII-style line-rate changes
 	 * for sub-10G clients.  Re-provision those rates to 10GBASE-R (XFI)
